1
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:27,230
Memories from ten years ago...

2
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:30,150
The words of the
man who was my dad...

3
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:36,670
Even if I was a mistake from the
beginning, the path I've chosen isn't.

4
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:42,579
I wanted that event to be
more than just a tragic backstory.

5
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:44,760
That's why I yearned to
become a champion of justice.

6
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:49,039
For over ten years,
I've clung to the ideal

7
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:53,200
of a world where everyone is
happy and no one needs to cry.

8
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:01,820
So it was clear from the
beginning what I needed to do.

9
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:06,770
I didn't fight because
I became a Master.

10
00:01:07,550 --> 00:01:12,829
I decided to fight because it
was something that I could do.

11
00:01:12,830 --> 00:01:14,390
Something I
believed I ought to do.

12
00:01:48,710 --> 00:01:49,720
Tohsaka...

13
00:02:09,990 --> 00:02:12,659
Hidden in my left hand

14
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:15,879
My wishes stay unfulfilled

15
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:20,590
Stuck in an unending dream

16
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:23,879
Hidden in my right hand

17
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:27,089
My hollow memories
stay invisible to all

18
00:02:27,090 --> 00:02:32,810
Being pelted by an unending rain

19
00:02:33,810 --> 00:02:38,960
Be it the strength to
protect what's precious

20
00:02:39,190 --> 00:02:43,459
Or the weakness
to lose faith in it

21
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:46,130
I'll accept it all

22
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:48,900
And look for a new dawn

23
00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:57,269
When I reach
out, I see the light

24
00:02:57,270 --> 00:03:02,520
In tatters, you
still save my life

25
00:03:02,670 --> 00:03:06,339
All the feelings
poured into the tip

26
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:08,839
Of the blade held aloft

27
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:16,290
A prayer that transcends time

28
00:03:31,230 --> 00:03:32,930
Where are you?

29
00:03:36,620 --> 00:03:40,920
Time of Departure

30
00:04:01,550 --> 00:04:03,519
How valiant.

31
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:06,589
You can continue to
defy me all you like,

32
00:04:06,590 --> 00:04:10,409
but your Servant
body cannot resist me.

33
00:04:10,410 --> 00:04:14,270
Surely you can sense my Command Spells
eating away at you, little by little.

34
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:19,560
Would it not be easier if you
simply gave in and submitted to me?

35
00:04:22,620 --> 00:04:24,540
Oh, my stubborn Saber...

36
00:04:25,290 --> 00:04:29,369
I'd like a girl like you.

37
00:04:29,370 --> 00:04:34,560
With gold hair, a small body,
young and noble-minded like a boy.

38
00:04:35,670 --> 00:04:39,540
It is admirable that you
choose death over betrayal.

39
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:43,500
I really want to trample on you.

40
00:04:45,270 --> 00:04:50,339
I will make you become
my Servant of your own will.

41
00:04:50,340 --> 00:04:55,180
Not your body, but I will start
by breaking down your heart.

42
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:59,130
What are you doing, Caster?

43
00:05:00,470 --> 00:05:02,050
Souichirou-sama...

44
00:05:02,470 --> 00:05:03,989
Why are you here?

45
00:05:03,990 --> 00:05:08,459
I thought I requested for you
to remain at Ryuudou Temple.

46
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:11,349
Answer my
question first, Caster.

47
00:05:11,350 --> 00:05:14,560
What are you doing here?

48
00:05:14,870 --> 00:05:19,870
Yesterday, I seized the Servant of
Emiya Shirou, one of the other Masters.

49
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:25,649
He escaped just before I could
finish him, but he is no longer a Master.

50
00:05:25,650 --> 00:05:27,169
I see.

51
00:05:27,170 --> 00:05:29,910
But I do not remember
instructing you to do so.

52
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:33,209
I acted on my own
authority, Master.

53
00:05:33,210 --> 00:05:37,359
I attacked this church in order
to obtain the Holy Grail's vessel

54
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:40,169
and slew the priest
who oversaw it,

55
00:05:40,170 --> 00:05:43,279
but the Grail's whereabouts
remain unknown.

56
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:47,050
You failed to return because
you couldn't locate the Grail?

57
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:50,709
I get the gist of the situation.

58
00:05:50,710 --> 00:05:52,810
Now, can you explain
why you acted on your own?

59
00:05:53,430 --> 00:05:55,160
I apologize.

60
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:58,479
However, my actions were
all for your sake, Master.

61
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:02,910
My only goal is to help
you achieve victory.

62
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:06,570
I have no other purpose.

63
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:08,270
I see.

64
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:11,950
In that case, you
cannot leave this place.

65
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:15,369
Search it until
you are satisfied.

66
00:06:15,370 --> 00:06:18,589
Until then, I will
also remain here.

67
00:06:18,590 --> 00:06:21,540
No, that will not be
necessary, Master.

68
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:25,170
Locating the Holy Grail
will take some time.

69
00:06:25,790 --> 00:06:30,009
It would be safer for you to
return to Ryuudou Temple.

70
00:06:30,010 --> 00:06:32,109
A fair point.

71
00:06:32,110 --> 00:06:35,270
But if I did so, I would be unable
to achieve my own objective.

72
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:38,100
Souichirou-sama, what is...

73
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:42,060
Be quick about it. If the
Grail isn't here, so be it.

74
00:06:42,530 --> 00:06:46,360
I don't care how you accomplish
this task. All I need is the result.

75
00:06:57,380 --> 00:07:01,260
When was it that I finally figured
out the true nature of that dream?

76
00:07:02,270 --> 00:07:06,590
That it was a certain Heroic
Spirit's mental landscape.

77
00:07:07,190 --> 00:07:10,709
Among the many Heroic
Spirits—the Servants...

78
00:07:10,710 --> 00:07:15,889
there are special Servants that
are safeguards, called "Guardians."

79
00:07:15,890 --> 00:07:20,140
They are summoned into the various ages
and prevent the human world's destruction.

80
00:07:21,990 --> 00:07:24,089
Or, more accurately,

81
00:07:24,090 --> 00:07:26,860
they counter the human
race's self-destruction.

82
00:07:27,830 --> 00:07:30,859
Even though he was
summoned to save humanity,

83
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:32,929
before he could save them,

84
00:07:32,930 --> 00:07:35,620
he was forced to shoulder
their countless mistakes.

85
00:07:37,490 --> 00:07:42,529
It didn't take long for him
to determine that it was futile

86
00:07:42,530 --> 00:07:44,939
and start despising
the human world.

87
00:07:44,940 --> 00:07:51,240
In the end, he continued to be
betrayed by his ideal, even after death.

88
00:08:05,060 --> 00:08:08,270
If you aren't feeling
well, we can put this off.

89
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:11,870
There's no pressing
need to attack right away.

90
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:17,260
No, if we know where Caster is,
we should deal with her at once.

91
00:08:20,540 --> 00:08:21,540
Here.

92
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:29,299
So you just watched me sleep instead
of waking me? That's kinda creepy.

93
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:31,069
Relax.

94
00:08:31,070 --> 00:08:33,949
I wouldn't dream of doing
something so improper.

95
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:36,140
I did overhear a
thing or two, though.

96
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:38,819
You muttered a few
rather harsh things,

97
00:08:38,820 --> 00:08:41,899
like "This is so irritating"
and "I'm pissed."

98
00:08:41,900 --> 00:08:43,720
Oh, that's a relief.

99
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:49,050
Say, Archer...

100
00:08:50,590 --> 00:08:54,020
Have you ever regretted
the things you've done?

101
00:08:55,550 --> 00:08:58,570
I want to do whatever I
can to avoid having regrets.

102
00:08:59,290 --> 00:09:02,379
That's probably easier
said than done, though.

103
00:09:02,380 --> 00:09:05,240
I bet it's even
harder than I imagine.

104
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:09,250
Some can do it, and some can't.

105
00:09:09,850 --> 00:09:12,399
You strike me as
the former type.

106
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:16,319
Not only do such people
rarely make mistakes,

107
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:19,170
they don't dwell
on the ones they do.

108
00:09:20,050 --> 00:09:21,050
Rin...

109
00:09:21,510 --> 00:09:25,520
Brilliant people shine more
brightly than ordinary ones.

110
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:30,460
They never regret or agonize
over what they've done.

111
00:09:31,210 --> 00:09:34,400
And you are most
definitely that sort of person.

112
00:09:35,140 --> 00:09:40,000
Tohsaka Rin can believe in her own
path to the very end without regret.

113
00:09:44,190 --> 00:09:45,820
What about you, then?

114
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:50,000
Will you be able to believe you made
the right choices until the very end?

115
00:09:50,490 --> 00:09:55,139
I'm sorry, but that
question is meaningless.

116
00:09:55,140 --> 00:09:56,260
Why?

117
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:59,010
Have you forgotten, Master?

118
00:09:59,590 --> 00:10:04,380
My "end" came and went long ago.

119
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:25,110
Jeez... Where the
heck has she gone to?

120
00:10:25,990 --> 00:10:28,970
Think hard about
where she is likely to go!

121
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:31,500
Damn it.

122
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:34,499
I don't have time
to cherry-pick.

123
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:36,520
He's the only person
she can rely on.

124
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:48,169
She attacked the overseer?
I'd say that's a bold move.

125
00:10:48,170 --> 00:10:51,660
Kirei was probably
prepared for it, though.

126
00:10:52,420 --> 00:10:54,770
Rin, I must ask you again.

127
00:10:55,180 --> 00:10:57,559
What, you're still worried?

128
00:10:57,560 --> 00:11:00,209
I'll take Caster on.

129
00:11:00,210 --> 00:11:04,150
If you get too close, she might
use Rule Breaker on you too.

130
00:11:04,590 --> 00:11:09,099
So I'll leave her
Master, Kuzuki, to you.

131
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:12,160
I'm fine with
taking on that man.

132
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:17,519
But do you understand that no
mage alive is a match for Caster?

133
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:21,170
Relax. If I didn't have a chance,
I wouldn't have suggested it.

134
00:11:21,620 --> 00:11:23,850
You can leave her to me, Archer.

135
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:28,930
Very well. I'll believe in you.

136
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:31,430
All right, let's do this.

137
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:34,310
I'll take out Caster
here, no matter what.

138
00:11:34,790 --> 00:11:37,353
And when I do, Saber will
probably return to normal

139
00:11:37,365 --> 00:11:39,940
and be able to forge a
new pact with Shirou, right?

140
00:12:03,270 --> 00:12:05,060
Did you kill Kirei?

141
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:07,049
Tohsaka...

142
00:12:07,050 --> 00:12:08,439
Yes.

143
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:12,800
Seemed like he was not going to
give me the Grail without protesting.

144
00:12:13,150 --> 00:12:14,999
That's good judgment.

145
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,890
So, did you make
sure he was dead?

146
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:20,810
Saber...

147
00:12:21,260 --> 00:12:23,439
And what is that
supposed to mean?

148
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:24,799
Nothing.

149
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,899
If you didn't see his corpse,

150
00:12:26,900 --> 00:12:29,610
he's still stubbornly clinging
to life somewhere. That's all.

151
00:12:29,910 --> 00:12:32,919
But enough about him.
Let's get this over with.

152
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:36,320
This time, you don't have a human
shield, so I can go all out to beat you.

153
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:40,370
Do you think you can beat
me in a battle of magic?

154
00:12:40,860 --> 00:12:42,899
It depends on how I go about it.

155
00:12:42,900 --> 00:12:46,079
And thankfully, you don't seem
to have full control of Saber yet.

156
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:49,010
Plus, I also know how
strong Kuzuki-sensei is.

157
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:51,840
He's no match for my Archer.

158
00:12:52,420 --> 00:12:54,529
Are you ready, Archer?

159
00:12:54,530 --> 00:12:55,590
I am.

160
00:12:56,310 --> 00:12:58,260
We proceed as
planned, then, Rin?

161
00:12:58,580 --> 00:12:59,599
Yes.

162
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:01,349
Don't hold back.

163
00:13:01,350 --> 00:13:03,680
I'm using everything I have!

164
00:13:09,150 --> 00:13:10,999
How adorable.

165
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,730
You think you have a chance
against me one-on-one?

166
00:13:16,470 --> 00:13:20,830
Are you forgetting
my trump card?

167
00:13:21,370 --> 00:13:26,500
With my Command Spells, I can
make her my puppet here and now.

168
00:13:26,920 --> 00:13:30,590
Were you to use one, Saber
would be able to resist it.

169
00:13:31,090 --> 00:13:33,759
I don't know if it would
be for one minute or two,

170
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:39,430
but that's more than enough
time to take down the likes of you!

171
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:55,600
A flash spell?

172
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:58,280
I'll start by dragging
you down to Earth!

173
00:14:01,830 --> 00:14:02,830
Archer!

174
00:14:16,020 --> 00:14:18,220
Huh? Archer?

175
00:14:27,750 --> 00:14:31,770
What do you think
you're doing, Archer?

176
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:37,950
You see, defeating her here
struck me as overly idealistic.

177
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:42,099
When it comes to escaping,
she's the best there is.

178
00:14:42,100 --> 00:14:47,260
She even tore apart her own
younger brother to get away.

179
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,879
You talk as though
you know all about me.

180
00:14:50,880 --> 00:14:53,880
Have you discerned
my true identity?

181
00:14:54,210 --> 00:14:56,819
Familiars that use
dragon teeth as vessels

182
00:14:56,820 --> 00:14:59,579
are the hallmark of the
King of Colchis's magic.

183
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:05,140
His daughter, Princess Medea,
was hailed as a witch without peer.

184
00:15:07,190 --> 00:15:08,890
He can't seriously be...

185
00:15:18,140 --> 00:15:24,830
If I may ask, Caster, do you
still have reserves to spare?

186
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:27,830
Archer, are you...

187
00:15:35,130 --> 00:15:36,759
Of course!

188
00:15:36,760 --> 00:15:42,149
I've stored sufficient mana to sustain
not only one more but all the Servants!

189
00:15:42,150 --> 00:15:43,930
Then that simplifies things.

190
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:48,610
I will take you up on
your earlier offer, Caster.

191
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:53,739
Even though you
turned me down before?

192
00:15:53,740 --> 00:15:55,549
The situation has changed.

193
00:15:55,550 --> 00:15:57,649
Considering the advantage
that Saber confers,

194
00:15:57,650 --> 00:16:00,110
isn't it only natural that
I should side with you?

195
00:16:03,500 --> 00:16:06,450
I distrust traitors.

196
00:16:06,860 --> 00:16:08,349
As well you should.

197
00:16:08,350 --> 00:16:11,729
I'm only yielding to
you for my own benefit.

198
00:16:11,730 --> 00:16:14,040
There is no trust
or loyalty in that.

199
00:16:14,560 --> 00:16:18,460
But is that not how
Servants are by nature?

200
00:16:20,140 --> 00:16:21,619
Very well.

201
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:27,139
I suppose I wouldn't be much of a
mage if I couldn't keep you under control.

202
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:31,190
Thus, I shall play
into your hands.

203
00:16:41,690 --> 00:16:42,820
Tohsaka!

204
00:16:56,250 --> 00:16:57,250
Trace...

205
00:16:58,130 --> 00:16:59,130
on!

206
00:17:11,930 --> 00:17:13,319
Shirou, you idiot!

207
00:17:13,320 --> 00:17:14,920
What do you think you're doing?

208
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:18,519
So that appears to be that.

209
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:20,449
Though I did not
expect your rude

210
00:17:20,461 --> 00:17:23,049
interruption, the outcome
remains unchanged.

211
00:17:23,050 --> 00:17:25,320
I shall finish you here.

212
00:17:25,770 --> 00:17:26,999
No.

213
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,420
Wait, Caster.

214
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:34,309
I want to attach one condition
to my joining your forces.

215
00:17:34,310 --> 00:17:36,420
A condition?

216
00:17:36,860 --> 00:17:39,949
I offered my freedom
without resistance.

217
00:17:39,950 --> 00:17:44,170
My price is that
you let them leave.

218
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:49,589
For all your words and
actions, you're rather soft.

219
00:17:49,590 --> 00:17:50,779
No.

220
00:17:50,780 --> 00:17:53,389
I merely thought it would
be wrong for a Heroic Spirit

221
00:17:53,390 --> 00:17:55,770
to cut down his
heartbroken former Master.

222
00:17:56,850 --> 00:18:01,590
It's strange to hear common
decency from a traitor's mouth.

223
00:18:04,060 --> 00:18:06,709
Very well. I shall let them go.

224
00:18:06,710 --> 00:18:09,660
But if they ever get
in my way again...

225
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:11,739
Of course.

226
00:18:11,740 --> 00:18:17,290
Fools who would embrace a hopeless
fight deserve to be cut down without mercy.

227
00:18:17,650 --> 00:18:18,929
Let's go.

228
00:18:18,930 --> 00:18:20,850
For now, he's right.

229
00:18:22,030 --> 00:18:24,869
Any anger you might hold
for me is misplaced, Rin.

230
00:18:24,870 --> 00:18:29,010
This woman is simply the
superior Master. That's all.

231
00:18:29,610 --> 00:18:32,010
I side with the most powerful.

232
00:18:32,370 --> 00:18:34,239
That's true.

233
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:36,229
But you'll regret it.

234
00:18:36,230 --> 00:18:38,369
I'll never quit.

235
00:18:38,370 --> 00:18:39,519
You hear me?

236
00:18:39,520 --> 00:18:42,310
I'll defeat Caster
and take you back.

237
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:44,690
And when I do,

238
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:48,110
no amount of apology
will be enough.

239
00:18:59,060 --> 00:19:01,099
That's what you get for
pulling a stunt like that!

240
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:03,090
Get some rest!

241
00:19:03,550 --> 00:19:07,279
No, let's get back to my
place as soon as possible.

242
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:09,339
It doesn't hurt that much.

243
00:19:09,340 --> 00:19:10,789
You can't be serious!

244
00:19:10,790 --> 00:19:14,150
Don't tell me it doesn't hurt,
not with an injury like that!

245
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:16,969
Hey, are you listening?

246
00:19:16,970 --> 00:19:19,879
Why is this even happening?

247
00:19:19,880 --> 00:19:22,559
Couldn't you tell right away
that the church wasn't safe?

248
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:25,669
I'm not that stupid.
Of course I could!

249
00:19:25,670 --> 00:19:27,859
Then you should have
turned right around, idiot!

250
00:19:27,860 --> 00:19:30,479
How could you try
projecting with those injuries?

251
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:33,189
You should've known
it'd just make them worse!

252
00:19:33,190 --> 00:19:36,079
And now you're telling
me you aren't in pain?

253
00:19:36,080 --> 00:19:38,610
What is wrong with you?

254
00:19:39,450 --> 00:19:42,330
Well, you're hurting
worse than I am, right?

255
00:19:43,880 --> 00:19:45,649
So let's go home.

256
00:19:45,650 --> 00:19:48,740
You can gripe and
moan once we get back.

257
00:19:56,590 --> 00:19:58,150
Uh...

258
00:19:58,960 --> 00:20:03,060
I can't believe this.
A guy made me cry.

259
00:20:05,820 --> 00:20:07,570
T-Tohsaka, my hand...

260
00:20:08,820 --> 00:20:09,919
Shut up.

261
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:11,610
You're going to
make this right, jerk.

262
00:20:17,600 --> 00:20:18,560
Listen,

263
00:20:18,561 --> 00:20:20,330
don't you dare turn around.

264
00:20:23,190 --> 00:20:25,830
If you see my face,
I'll get really mad.

265
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:32,090
Archer was right.

266
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:36,980
I should have defeated Caster when I
had the chance, no matter what it took.

267
00:20:37,970 --> 00:20:40,380
I'm not whining or anything,

268
00:20:41,140 --> 00:20:45,390
but I always mess up
the most important thing.

269
00:20:46,110 --> 00:20:50,290
I can handle the second or
third most important thing easily.

270
00:20:51,060 --> 00:20:54,110
But I always mess up
the most important one.

271
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:58,750
I can't only blame him
for going over to her side.

272
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:01,469
Sheesh.

273
00:21:01,470 --> 00:21:03,280
After all I said,

274
00:21:04,330 --> 00:21:06,210
I suddenly found
myself cornered.

275
00:21:09,340 --> 00:21:13,439
I think this is where you're
supposed to say, "By what?"

276
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:14,449
Oh.

277
00:21:14,450 --> 00:21:17,140
Then, cornered by what?

278
00:21:17,780 --> 00:21:22,770
By you. Your words made me realize
I'd failed, and I got even more depressed.

279
00:21:23,500 --> 00:21:25,859
That's only temporary, right?

280
00:21:25,860 --> 00:21:28,980
You haven't done anything
to beat yourself up over.

281
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:30,670
Why not?

282
00:21:31,320 --> 00:21:35,330
We're in this mess because
my strategy was so wrong.

283
00:21:36,220 --> 00:21:39,679
That just means you
failed at one thing.

284
00:21:39,680 --> 00:21:41,760
But that doesn't mean
you're wrong, Tohsaka.

285
00:21:44,290 --> 00:21:48,000
To be honest, you look
blindingly brilliant to me.

286
00:21:48,370 --> 00:21:50,060
I don't regret things, either.

287
00:21:50,660 --> 00:21:54,650
I believe what I've
done to be right, but...

288
00:21:55,590 --> 00:21:58,010
That belief is a
mess of patches.

289
00:21:58,630 --> 00:22:01,689
But once you get that
regret out of your system,

290
00:22:01,690 --> 00:22:04,350
I bet you'll pay
them back twice over.

291
00:22:09,410 --> 00:22:12,870
By the way, why did you save me?

292
00:22:17,080 --> 00:22:19,560
Huh? How did you get that?

293
00:22:20,360 --> 00:22:22,110
You can have it back.

294
00:22:22,710 --> 00:22:26,480
I have another pendant
just like it at my house.

295
00:22:27,100 --> 00:22:31,749
After Lancer nearly killed me at
school, I found it lying next to me.

296
00:22:31,750 --> 00:22:33,170
I've had it ever since.

297
00:22:33,940 --> 00:22:36,540
You have one just like it?

298
00:22:38,760 --> 00:22:41,220
Huh? Did I say
something strange?

299
00:22:42,250 --> 00:22:44,159
No, not really.

300
00:22:44,160 --> 00:22:48,800
Anyway, why would this be
a reason for you to save me?

301
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:51,190
Well...

302
00:22:57,630 --> 00:22:59,700
The truth is, that
was an afterthought.

303
00:23:00,440 --> 00:23:01,440
If I must confess,

304
00:23:01,930 --> 00:23:05,950
I've always been attracted to
this girl named Tohsaka Rin.

305
00:23:06,220 --> 00:23:08,250
Then, inconvenient as it was...

306
00:23:09,180 --> 00:23:13,870
When I finally got around to
talking to her, I fell for her even more.

307
00:23:14,670 --> 00:23:18,820
So before I knew it, I had already
jumped down there without thinking.

308
00:23:21,560 --> 00:23:25,339
H-Hey, if you go around blurting
out things like that without thinking,

309
00:23:25,340 --> 00:23:27,929
people will get the wrong idea!

310
00:23:27,930 --> 00:23:31,149
I really do have
feelings for you!

311
00:23:31,150 --> 00:23:34,020
Y-You jerk! You enormous jerk!

312
00:23:42,910 --> 00:23:45,329
Thanks for coming to my rescue.

313
00:23:45,330 --> 00:23:48,240
You're a lifesaver.

314
00:24:01,480 --> 00:24:07,099
If I am destined to
turn to ash and bones

315
00:24:07,100 --> 00:24:11,230
Then I want to sing of
happiness and despair

316
00:24:11,250 --> 00:24:19,250
While I still can

317
00:24:22,990 --> 00:24:28,659
Our fate for the days to come

318
00:24:28,660 --> 00:24:35,719
Is fighting an inch from death

319
00:24:35,720 --> 00:24:43,720
With dreams in our hearts

320
00:24:44,010 --> 00:24:48,219
Once you cried at night

321
00:24:48,220 --> 00:24:56,220
But a better future for
us was always possible

322
00:24:56,430 --> 00:25:00,999
Quietude awaits you

323
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:07,279
We can find that gleaming hill

324
00:25:07,280 --> 00:25:12,889
Ring your bell

325
00:25:12,890 --> 00:25:19,630
Towards your own horizon

326
00:25:23,670 --> 00:25:26,959
I appreciate your
thoughtfulness, but before that...

327
00:25:26,960 --> 00:25:29,799
It works best when the
raw materials are fresh.

328
00:25:29,800 --> 00:25:32,469
Could we work
with other Masters?

329
00:25:32,470 --> 00:25:35,585
You are about to die here,
so is that any of your concern?

330
00:25:35,586 --> 00:25:37,980
The Princess of Colchis

331
00:25:34,350 --> 00:25:37,980
Next Time

